{"agent":"Monster3-SQ-priority-fair-queue-7267fe","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"`_eta` computes `running_left_s` from only slots where `_held` is true, so it ignores idle slots. If `slots_n` is larger than the number of held slots, the earliest available slot is immediately free, but `_eta` still passes the minimum remaining time of the held slots. For example, with `slots_n=2`, slot 0 held with note `{\"cost_s\": 600, \"at\": now}`, slot 1 free, and waiting line `[a, b]`, `_eta` passes `running_left_s=600` for `b`; `SQ.estimate` therefore adds a 10-minute offset even though slot 1 is idle and `a` can start now. The ETA is wrong (overestimated) whenever at least one slot is free while another held slot has a positive estimate.","digest":"a6988df011890d7b","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/services/suitelock.py:_eta","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/suitelock.py:_eta"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"The `contextlib.suppress(OSError, ValueError, TypeError)` around the held-slot note read does not cover a missing `at` key. Given a slot note file containing `{\"cost_s\": 100}` (or `{}`), `_held` can be true, `json.loads` succeeds, `held.get(\"cost_s\")` succeeds, then `float(held[\"at\"])` raises `KeyError`, which is not suppressed and propagates. This crashes the queue-status/Blocked path instead of treating the note as unreadable, even though the code explicitly tries to tolerate malformed slot notes.","digest":"778c5367b7e7cbaf","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/services/suitelock.py:_eta","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/suitelock.py:_eta"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"A held slot whose note lacks `cost_s` is treated as having zero seconds left. Given a held slot note `{\"at\": now-1}` with no `cost_s`, `held.get(\"cost_s\") or 0.0` yields `0.0`, so `left` receives `0` and `running_left_s` becomes `0`. The estimate then says a running suite will free a slot immediately even though it may run for hours. Missing predicted cost should fall back to a default or be skipped, not be interpreted as “about to finish now.”","digest":"ff527e0777a636cb","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/services/suitelock.py:_eta","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/services/suitelock.py:_eta"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"When `_note_of` returns `None`—a case the new code explicitly handles with `(mine or (\"\", 0.0))[1]` and `if mine is not None:`—the slot note is written with `cost_s: 0.0`. The code then still calls `_eta(line, name, slots_n, directory)` to build the `SuiteBusy` estimate. Thus a holder whose class/scope cannot be estimated is advertised as having zero remaining work. For example, if no `[suites].class_patterns` match holder `agent:foo` (or the cost lookup yields `None`), it can hold a suite slot for 30 minutes, but a waiter behind it sees the holder note with `cost_s=0.0` and the ETA calculation treats that slot as already free, so the busy line reports an estimated wait of 0m or otherwise far too low. The `default_cost_s` knob exists for missing estimates, but this path bypasses it and uses zero.","digest":"dea73eef93ee2d24","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/services/suitelock.py:suite_lock","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/suitelock.py:suite_lock"},{"chunk":4,"detail":"The fair-share stage can let one agent take all offered slots. Example: `slots=2`, `agent_share=0.2`, and six waiting tickets: five short `item` tickets from agent `A` (`cost_s=1`) plus one long `item` ticket from agent `B` (`cost_s=100000`). `cap=max(1, math.ceil(0.2*6))=2`; the short A tickets sort first, so `kept` receives A1, A2, B and the remaining A tickets are deferred, yielding an order beginning `A1, A2, B, ...`. Filling two slots from that order gives both slots to A. With one slot and a continuous supply of short A tickets, B is kept behind the current A ticket after each recomputation and can be delayed arbitrarily by choosing a large `max_wait_factor`/`cost_s`, so the “fair share” cap on the current waiting list does not actually bound slot allocation or prevent starvation.","digest":"70f23fc34d050c40","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/services/suitequeue.py:order","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/suitequeue.py:order"},{"chunk":4,"detail":"The aging bound is not honored once fair share is applied. Example: `max_wait_factor=1`, `agent_share=0.2`, `default_cost_s=10`, and waiting tickets `A1` (`cost_s=10`, `waited_s=100`) and `A2` (`cost_s=10`, `waited_s=10`) from agent `A`, plus `B1`, `C1`, `D1` (`cost_s=1000`, `waited_s=0`) from different agents. Both A tickets are overdue (`10 >= 1*10`), but `cap=1`, so the returned order is `A1, B1, C1, D1, A2`. With `slots=2`, the second slot goes to non-overdue `B1` while overdue `A2` waits, directly contradicting the module contract that an overdue ticket “goes first” and “nothing waits past that bound whatever arrives behind it.”","digest":"f69d5d886ad66c5f","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/services/suitequeue.py:order","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/suitequeue.py:order"},{"chunk":4,"detail":"`estimate` uses raw `Waiting.cost_s` for both the wait and the predicted run, but the module contract says a cost of `0` means unknown and counts as `default_cost_s`. Because `estimate` has no `default_cost_s` parameter, an ordered queue in which every ticket has `cost_s=0.0` (unknown measured cost) returns `wait_s=0.0` and `predicted_s=0.0` for the last ticket when `slots=1` and `running_left_s=0.0`, even though each unknown ticket should contribute the configured default (for example, 60 seconds). This underestimates the ETA for queues of tickets whose cost has not yet been measured.","digest":"42f743d0d6a4eb2f","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/services/suitequeue.py:estimate","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/suitequeue.py:estimate"},{"chunk":6,"detail":"Given `waiting = [W(\"a\", cost=600), W(\"b\", cost=300), W(\"me\", cost=60)]`, `slots=2`, and `running_left_s=0.0`, line 84 asserts `two[\"wait_s\"] == 450.0`. With two free slots, the two tickets ahead of `me` can both start immediately; `me` can start as soon as the shorter of the two ahead tickets finishes, i.e. after 300 seconds. The asserted 450 seconds is therefore a 150-second overestimate and encodes an estimate that can idle an available slot from 300s to 450s.","digest":"5b7e114c4c9a9218","family":"alibaba","location":"tests/test_suite_queue_priority.py:84","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_suite_queue_priority.py:84"}],"chunks_total":6,"coverage":"6/6 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":30330,"diff_sha":"b8f4d1c24bc30f6592997a1b35e2b6b720266487774a000cc46fd6009276e1a5","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/SQ-priority-fair-queue","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":551.5,"excluded_bytes":1147,"excluded_files":1,"excluded_paths":["README.md"],"family":"alibaba","findings":8,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"[REDACTED:name]","output_digest":"0838a94b46d83188","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/SQ-priority-fair-queue.rubber_duck.[REDACTED:name].20261112T164242Z-9c29b23c.jsonl","reason":"","review_degraded":[{"at":1794502314.1120958,"family":"google","gate":"rubber_duck","model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","reason":"HTTP 429","reviewer":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite"},{"at":1794502314.3993685,"family":"xai","gate":"rubber_duck","model":"grok-4.7","reason":"HTTP 403","reviewer":"grok-4.7"}],"review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4,5,6],"reviewed_for_holder":"[REDACTED:hostname]-SQ-priority-fair-queue-7267fe 